-- title:
--   Degree is homogeneous of degree 2g on endomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, $A$ a scheme and $f : A \to \operatorname{Spec} K$ a morphism, and let $L$ be a relative group law on $f$: a group structure on the set $\{\varphi : T \to A \mid \varphi \circ f = t\}$ of $T$-points for every $K$-scheme $(T,t)$, given by operations `mul`, `one`, `inv` satisfying associativity, the unit laws and left inverses, and natural in the base in the sense that multiplication commutes with precomposition by any $\psi : T' \to T$ with $\psi$ followed by $t$ equal to $t'$. Assume $L$ is commutative, and that $f$ satisfies `AbelianSchemePropertyBundle`: $f$ is smooth and proper, the fibre $f^{-1}(s)$ over every point $s$ of $\operatorname{Spec} K$ is connected, and $f$ admits a relative group law. Fix $g \in \mathbb{N}$ with $f$ smooth of relative dimension $g$, a finite index type $\iota$, and a family $\alpha : \iota \to \{\beta : A \to A \mid \beta \circ f = f\}$ of endomorphisms of $A$ over $K$ such that each $\alpha_i$ is a homomorphism for the group law, i.e. $(x \cdot y)$ followed by $\alpha_i$ equals $(x$ followed by $\alpha_i) \cdot (y$ followed by $\alpha_i)$ for all $T$-points $x,y$ over any $(T,t)$. Then there is a homogeneous polynomial $P \in \mathbb{Q}[X_i : i \in \iota]$ of degree $2g$ such that for every $n : \iota \to \mathbb{Z}$ the natural number $L.\mathrm{endDegree}\bigl(\prod_i \alpha_i^{n_i}\bigr)$, the product being taken in the commutative group of endomorphisms of $A$ over $K$ induced by $L$, equals $P\bigl((n_i)_i\bigr)$ in $\mathbb{Q}$. Here $\mathrm{endDegree}(\beta)$ is the $K$-dimension at the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} K$ of the kernel scheme, the fibre product of $\beta$ and the unit section, when that kernel is finite over $K$, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the statement that the degree of an endomorphism of an abelian variety extends to a homogeneous polynomial function of degree $2g$ on the group generated by finitely many endomorphisms (Mumford, *Abelian Varieties*, §19, Theorem 2), here in the functor-of-points formulation with the degree defined as the order of the kernel scheme. It is used in the degree theory for endomorphisms of fake elliptic curves and of Jacobians, for instance in the resultant description of the order of kernels of polynomials in the Frobenius and in the bounds on endomorphism degrees of quaternionic abelian surfaces.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_GoodReductionJacobian_RelativeGroupLaw_exists_isHomogeneous_eval_eq_endDegree_of_abelianSchemePropertyBundle.lean

